* L1_RECT_model.lib -- three interchangeable implementations of the same
* L1_RECT_MODEL subckt (same name + pin interface in every section):
*   ideal  : single ideal inductor, L=2.5024n
*   rl     : EM-derived series L+R, L=2.5024n R=3.1218ohm
*   snp2le : snp2le broadband vector-fitted macromodel (same EM data)
* Select the active one from the including file via:
*   .lib <path>/L1_RECT_model.lib ideal   (or rl, or snp2le)
*
* L1 (lna_core_cg's cascode source-degeneration inductor) is EM-characterized
* as its own rectangular coil (L1_RECT_coil.gds, outer_half_x=244.5,
* outer_half_y=151.0, N=2/W=26/S=2um) -- previously L1 had no dedicated
* model at all and simply reused LSHUNT_OUT_model.sym/.lib directly (same
* 2.5041nH target, deliberately shared value -- see the floorplan-fit
* report), since the layout choice of which physical coil GDS to draw is
* independent of which SPICE model the schematic references (LVS strips
* inductors entirely, per check_lna_core_layouts.py). Once L1 got its own,
* differently-shaped physical layout to fit the 1070x1070 macro budget, its
* own EM-extracted L/R started to differ slightly from LSHUNT_OUT's
* (2.5024nH/3.1218ohm vs LSHUNT_OUT's 2.5041nH/3.0693ohm -- same target,
* different parasitics from the different aspect ratio), so it gets its own
* model file here for electrical accuracy in the real simulated schematic
* (xschem/lna_core.sch) and the per-block LVS-reference one
* (xschem/lna_core_cg.sch) -- both now instantiate L1_RECT_model.sym
* instead of LSHUNT_OUT_model.sym.

.lib ideal
.SUBCKT L1_RECT_MODEL p1 p2
L1 p1 p2 2.5024n
.ENDS L1_RECT_MODEL
.endl ideal

.lib rl
.SUBCKT L1_RECT_MODEL p1 p2
R1 p1 mid_L1_RECT 3.1218
L1 mid_L1_RECT p2 2.5024n
.ENDS L1_RECT_MODEL
.endl rl

.lib snp2le
